0..76 Comment "// Dybjer and Setzer\'s codes for inductive-recursive definitions, as data. A"
77..128 Comment "// function gives the arguments each code asks for."
129..131 Comment "//"
132..203 Comment "// A code describes a family and its decoder at once. A code asks for a"
204..278 Comment "// value of a type, for values of the family, or for a stop. The values of"
279..347 Comment "// the family come through their decodes. A stop names one decode. A"
348..424 Comment "// function computes the type of these arguments from the code. A family and"
425..472 Comment "// its decoder thus follow from the code alone."
473..475 Comment "//"
476..552 Comment "// The codes are a large type. A field of a code holds a type. The pairs are"
553..629 Comment "// data. The function `args` returns them as terms. It recurses on the code."
630..704 Comment "// The delta arm asks for a function into the family. The rest of the code"
705..752 Comment "// reads that function through the decoder `t`."
753..755 Comment "//"
756..836 Comment "// - see: #3575 — not implemented: the family a code defines, with its decoder"
837..916 Comment "// - see: `pathological/universe/ir-codes.gandr` — the family a code defines,"
917..975 Comment "//   its decoder, and the decode of its arguments, refused"
976..1052 Comment "// - see: Dybjer and Setzer, _A finite axiomatization of inductive-recursive"
1053..1111 Comment "//   definitions_, TLCA 1999, doi:10.1007/3-540-48959-2_11"
1113..1169 Comment "/// The dependent pairs over a family of types, as data."
